```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Worker
  participant RetrySvc
  participant DB
  participant XAPI

  Worker->>DB: pick failed posts with next_scheduled_at <= now
  loop for each failed post
    Worker->>RetrySvc: request attempt(postId)
    RetrySvc->>DB: get attempt metadata (attempts, idempotency_key)
    RetrySvc->>XAPI: POST /create (with idempotency_key)
    alt success
      XAPI-->>RetrySvc: 200/201
      RetrySvc->>DB: mark SENT, store remote_post_id
    else transient failure (e.g., 429)
      XAPI-->>RetrySvc: 429 Retry-After
      RetrySvc->>DB: increment attempt, set next_scheduled_at (backoff)
    else permanent failure
      RetrySvc->>DB: mark FAILED (do not reschedule automatically)
    end
  end

  Note over RetrySvc: Default backoff: 1m, 5m, 15m (configurable by ops)
```

Sequence diagram describing retry attempts, backoff, and idempotency handling.
